      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Topological quantum error correction and surface-code ideas made fault-tolerant quantum computation a concrete physical program, linking quantum information to many-body physics and topology.",
        "attribution": "Kitaev's foundational code and topological ideas, Preskill's development of the fault-tolerance framework, and Bravyi's major code-theory contributions are important, though the field's conceptual lineage is broad.",
        "maturity": "The theory is well developed and experimental demonstrations have advanced, but large-scale fault-tolerant operation remains unproven.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The ultimate scientific standing of the field depends partly on whether fault-tolerant devices achieve reliable operation at scale.",
          "The candidate label combines related theoretical developments whose attribution may not map cleanly to three individuals."
        ]
      }
